course: dictionary
lesson: 7107
title: Context clues: peat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Peat is a word you may not know, but the sentences around it give clues. «Peat is partly rotted plant matter in bogs» tells you it is made of plants. Then «was burned for fuel» tells you people used it to make fires.
explain: Look for clue words like «mostly bog moss» and «in cold, wet, acid, airless bogs». They show peat is a soft soil made of plants that rot very slowly in wet places. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning in place of the hard word and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words in a text are about the same thing. «Peatlands cover only about 3 percent of the land» tells you peatlands are areas where peat is found. Peat is not coal yet: «the first step towards coal» means it comes before coal.
fact: Peat is soft, dark brown soil made of plants that have half-rotted very slowly.
fact: Peat forms in wet, boggy places over thousands of years.
fact: «Peat» can be dried and burned as fuel.
fact: Peat grows only about 1 millimetre a year, because rotting is very slow in cold, wet bogs.
fact: Peatlands store more carbon than all the world's forests together, so protecting them helps the climate.
exercise: «The people cut peat and burned it on their fires.» What is peat used for? | Building houses | Growing tall trees | *Fuel for fires | Making bread
exercise: Peat forms in wet, boggy places. Where would you most likely find peat? | *A boggy, wet place | A dry desert | A busy motorway | The top of a mountain
exercise: «Peatlands cover only about 3 percent of the land.» What are peatlands? | *Areas of land where peat is found | Large, dry deserts | Very tall hills | Places where people sell cakes
test: «Peat grows only about 1 millimetre a year.» What does this tell you about how peat forms? | It never forms at all | *It forms very slowly, over many years | It forms very quickly, in a few days | It forms only on the sea floor
test: Nadia says peat means the same as coal. Is she right? | Yes, peat and coal are exactly the same | *No, peat comes before coal and is not coal itself | No, peat is a kind of bird | Yes, because both are black rock
exam: Which phrase in «Peat is partly rotted plant matter in bogs, the first step towards coal, and was burned for fuel» tells you people could use peat to make fires? | the first step towards coal | *was burned for fuel | in bogs | partly rotted
